This function does not require any coding, but can be coded if automation is required.

Link: https://functioninfosec.azurewebsites.net/api/Securekeys
The result will be a hex encoded, min-entropy CSNBRNG 256 bit perfect (pre tested) key.
The prime purpose is to use with legacy system like AES until migration to One Cipher and One Link ciphers.

Note: Until the end of August 2026 this function requires no infrastructure subscription to use.
